      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): create catalog sessions from the sidebar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nUsers could not start provider-native sessions from a session catalog header, and a Claude Code session created through OpenClaw could appear twice: once under Claude Code and again under the owning agent's Chats group.\n\nThe sidebar also made agent ownership difficult to scan because nested session rows lacked a clear hierarchy and session creation was detached from the agent it targeted.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds an optional catalog-provided session creation capability.\n- Opens the existing `/new` workflow from catalog headers using only an opaque catalog ID.\n- Resolves the catalog label and model from the gateway-advertised capability instead of URL parameters.\n- Keeps catalog-targeted drafts on the default agent whose runtime policy was validated.\n- Adds per-agent creation actions and clearer hierarchy styling.\n- Links Claude CLI-backed OpenClaw sessions to catalog rows so the duplicate Chats presentation is suppressed.\n\nThe backing OpenClaw session remains intact for execution; only its duplicate sidebar presentation is removed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can create a session from an agent row or the Claude Code catalog header, retain the normal folder, worktree, and execution-node controls, and see Claude Code sessions only under Claude Code.\n\nCatalog-targeted drafts show the gateway-advertised runtime and do not allow switching to an agent with a different runtime policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 56 focused protocol, Anthropic catalog, sidebar, location, and create-parameter tests passed.\n- All 7 new-session browser E2E tests passed, including a spoofed URL model and non-default agent regression case.\n- UI, extension production, and extension test typechecks passed.\n- Oxfmt and Oxlint passed on the touched files.\n- Existing LOC ratchets remain unchanged.\n- AWS Crabbox exact-head proof passed on `5f90aa0cae`.\n- Trusted structured autoreview reported no actionable findings.\n",
        "branch": "fix/sidebar-agent-session-hierarchy",
